s://github.com/gabe4coding/claude-code-mode/pull/47#discussion_r4313241737\">\u25b6</a>\n2. <img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;<img alt=\"Security\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Security.svg?v=2\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Brace spellings skip approval** <a href=\"https://github.com/gabe4coding/claude-code-mode/pull/47#discussion_r4313241748\">\u25b6</a>\n3. <img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;<img alt=\"Security\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Security.svg?v=2\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Relative deletions skip approval** <a href=\"https://github.com/gabe4coding/claude-code-mode/pull/47#discussion_r4313241756\">\u25b6</a>\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Summary</h3></summary>\n\nThe PR broadens the Bash guard to catch common shell spellings and bumps the plugin to `0.12.6`.\n- Bash commands now catch common spellings of protected hint and function folders.\n</details>\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Diagram</h3></summary>\n\n```mermaid\n%%{init: {'theme': 'neutral'}}%%\nflowchart TD\n  A[Bash command] --> B[Split words and fold paths]\n  B --> C[Check relative paths after cd]\n  C --> D[Check protected names and read-only exception]\n  D --> E{Protected path found?}\n  E -->|Yes| F[Deny command]\n  E -->|No| G[Forward command to Bash]\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:0 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (2) \u00b7 Last reviewed commit: [\"Bash guard: close the spellings the revi...\"](https://github.com/gabe4coding/claude-code-mode/commit/5075dbc6918a73c32ed780236d3812bd007318f7) \u00b7 [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_review&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=review_public&utm_content=gabe4coding/claude-code-mode)</sub>\n"
